cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use virtual-fly in research, please cite the software release and its archived DOI when available."
title: "virtual-fly: a connectome-initialized, plastic virtual Drosophila in closed loop"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - name: "shute2004"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shute2004/virtual-fly"
url: "https://github.com/shute2004/virtual-fly"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A connectome-initialized virtual adult male Drosophila system that evolves
  MaleCNS neural activity, neuromodulation, and local synaptic plasticity in
  closed loop with a FlyBody/MuJoCo physical body and environment. Canonical
  experiment v1 provides a pinned, provenance-tracked reference run and an
  end-to-end reproducer; the short canonical run demonstrates stored-weight
  changes under the current local-plasticity semantics but does not establish
  categorical behavioral improvement.
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - computational neuroscience
  - neuromodulation
  - synaptic plasticity
  - embodied simulation
  - MuJoCo
  - reproducible research
